+# CODEX Render Master Control Patch
+
+This patch implements the changes requested in your last two messages:
+
+1) **Webhook pendings (WAITING rows) show SL/TP as distances** rather than fixed prices.
+2) The **manual Alerts backup/restore UI button is removed** from the dashboard.
+3) **Autostart can be set to start ALL scripts** after deploy (with an optional exclude list).
+4) **Triggered webhook pendings no longer linger/duplicate** broker orders in the Open Orders / Positions table.
+
+---
+
+## What you should see after applying
+
+### A) Webhook pending rows (Type=webhook, Status=WAITING)
+- The **Stop Loss** and **Take Profit** columns show **distance from entry**:
+  - `abs(stop_loss - entry_price)`
+  - `abs(take_profit - entry_price)`
+- Once the webhook triggers and the order is created, the pending row is **no longer included** in `/api/open-orders`.
+
+### B) No more duplicate/clutter after the webhook triggers
+- When the pending webhook triggers, the dashboard should show only the real broker objects:
+  - the **Position** (OPEN)
+  - the **SL** and **TP** orders (Untriggered)
+- The old “calc_crypto_..._short_market” (or similar) row should **not remain**.
+
+### C) Dashboard toolbar
+- Only **Refresh** remains (the **Alerts backup/restore** button is removed).
+
+### D) Autostart behavior
+- Default remains: `bybit_monitor,oanda_monitor,fxweekend-clone`
+- New option:
+  - `AUTOSTART_SCRIPTS=ALL` (or `*`) starts every discovered script
+  - `AUTOSTART_EXCLUDE=name1,name2` skips specific scripts
+
+---
+
+## Files changed
+
+### Backend
+- `render/master_service.py`
+  - Autostart: adds `ALL/*` support and `AUTOSTART_EXCLUDE`
+  - Pending webhooks:
+    - enforce `broker=WEBHOOK` and `type=webhook`
+    - on successful broker order creation, mark pending webhook `TRIGGERED` + `enabled=False` instead of mutating into a broker order row
+    - `/api/open-orders` includes **only** pending webhooks where `status=WAITING` and `enabled=true`
+  - Dashboard HTML: removes the Alerts backup/restore button and changes watchlist subtext to “Saved locally”
+
+### Front-end
+- `render/static/dashboard.js`
+  - removes Alerts backup/restore modal + event bindings
+  - for webhook WAITING rows, renders SL/TP as distances
+
+- `render/static/open_orders.js`
+  - for webhook WAITING rows, renders SL/TP as distances
+
+---
+
+## How to apply
+
+You have a unified diff file (`.diff`). From the repo root (the folder that contains `render/`):
+
+```bash
+# 1) Backup (recommended)
+cp -a . ../CODEX-backup-before-patch
+
+# 2) Apply the patch
+patch -p1 < codex_render_master_patch.diff
+
+# 3) Deploy
+# Push to GitHub / redeploy Render as you normally do
+```
+
+If `patch` reports offsets, that’s fine as long as it applies cleanly.
+
+---
+
+## Render environment variables
+
+### Default autostart (unchanged)
+No change needed.
+
+### Start everything
+Set:
+- `AUTOSTART_SCRIPTS=ALL`
+
+Optional excludes:
+- `AUTOSTART_EXCLUDE=scriptA,scriptB`
+
+Notes:
+- Starting *everything* can be unsafe if some scripts are intended to run only on-demand. Use `AUTOSTART_EXCLUDE` to avoid that.
+
+---
+
+## Implementation notes (why this fixes the duplication)
+
+Previously, when a webhook triggered, the code updated the pending webhook entry to look like a Bybit/OANDA order (changing `broker`/`type`/`status`).
+
+At the same time, `/api/open-orders` was already pulling real broker orders from Bybit/OANDA.
+
+So you ended up with:
+- the real broker orders/position **plus**
+- a “fake” broker order row sourced from `pending_webhooks.json`
+
+This patch fixes that by:
+- keeping pending webhooks local-only (`WEBHOOK/webhook`)
+- marking them consumed (`TRIGGERED`, `enabled=false`)
+- and only returning `WAITING` pendings in `/api/open-orders`.
